@name Explainer 5: achromatic landscape lens 50mm f/14
# Explainer #5: achromatic landscape lens (Wollaston 1812 / Chevalier): the
# doublet of #4 bent into a meniscus, concave towards a stop in front of it.
# Role: moving the stop fixes the corners (coma, field curvature) but
# brings barrel distortion.
# Design: three curvatures, both glass thicknesses and the stop distance
# vary (EFL 50 mm), minimising the white-light RMS spot at 0, 0.5, 0.7 and
# 1.0 of the field, object at 2.5 m.
# Rows match 04-achromat (stop first) so the video can morph them.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/05-landscape.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/14, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 3.3, 0.5: 10.3, 0.7: 18.1, 1: 32.2 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
  stop        8.3899      air            1.787
  -45.8641    4.0000      N-BK7          4.410
  -8.9515     1.5000      F2             5.650
  -15.1064    42.0000     air            6.700
